>addressof</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>base<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Reference-to-const that refers to the current element. The result may be a prvalue (e.g. if <code>*base()</code> is a prvalue).</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Pointer-to-const that points to the current element.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/basic_const_iterator/operator_at\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>operator[]</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  accesses an element by index <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"iterator","title":"Iterator library"},{"path":"iterator/basic_const_iterator","title":"std::basic_const_iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_const_iterator<Iter>::operator*","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Returns a reference or pointer to the const version of the current element."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Reference-to-const that refers to the current element. The result may be a prvalue (e.g. if *base() is a prvalue)."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"operator[]","note":"accesses an ele